# Copy to `.env.production` for a local production build (`npm run build`,
# `npm run worker:dev`, `npm run deploy`). Not needed for `npm run dev`, which
# Vite never loads this file for.
#
# Nothing here is a secret. A Turnstile site key is public by design: Vite
# inlines it into the JS bundle and Turnstile renders it into the page, so
# every visitor already has it. It is ignored by git because a deploy does not
# read it, not because it is sensitive - see below.
#
# THE DEPLOY DOES NOT USE THIS FILE. Deploys build on Cloudflare from a push to
# main, where this file does not exist. The value that ships comes from the
# build variable of the same name, set in the dashboard under
#   Workers & Pages > msicard-portfolio > Settings > Build > Variables
# Vite merges process.env over .env files, so if both exist the build variable
# is the one that wins. Keep them in step or expect to be confused.
#
# Take the value from Cloudflare dashboard > Turnstile > your widget. Its
# matching SECRET key is not a build variable and never belongs in any file:
# it is a Worker secret, TURNSTILE_SECRET. See .dev.vars.example.
#
# scripts/check-build.mjs fails any deploying build where this is missing or
# set to one of Cloudflare's test keys.
VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=""
